  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving the wellbeing of displaced population in Borena zone, Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2,700 older people and people with disabilities have access to improved sanitation facilities through the construction of 22 latrines and 10 handwashing facilities</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">200 older people and people with disabilities headed households have access to WASH NFI kits</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conduct 192 awareness raising sessions to promote improved hygiene and sanitation practices and COVID-19 mitigation measures</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HelpAge International has identified significant needs in accessing WASH facilities and low awareness around safe hygiene practices. This project will be imlemented in Guchi , allowing to reach a greater number of people among the IDP&apos;s and host community population.This project will benefit a total of 9,960 (4598 male and 5,362 female) IDPs and host community memebers surrounding the eight targeted idp sites.</narrative>
  </description>
